{
  "id": "independent-self-construal",
  "term": "independent self-construal",
  "definition": "Independent self-construal is a way of understanding oneself in which outside influences such as luck are treated more as temporary personal states than as support rooted in social relationships. In the source, this means people with an independent self-construal are less likely to see luck as a stable basis for confidence in later decisions.",
